# /usr/share/icons/Orion-X-Cursor/index.theme
# Orion-X Phoenix Edition — cursor theme (placeholder)
#
# @decision DEC-PHASE11-010
# @title W11-9b: Orion-X-Cursor placeholder — Adwaita inheritance, polish deferred
# @status accepted
# @rationale This is a naming-only shim so CursorTheme=Orion-X-Cursor in
#   the xsettings.xml resolves cleanly. Full cursor resolution falls through to
#   Adwaita (already installed as part of the GNOME/GTK3 base packages).
#   No cursor pixmaps are shipped in this W11-9b slice — cursor visual polish
#   (actual Phoenix-tinted cursors) is deferred to a follow-up rider sub-slice.
#   The rider sub-slice will provide:
#     - /usr/share/icons/Orion-X-Cursor/cursors/ directory with
#       X11 binary cursor files in Bibata-Modern-Ice or custom Phoenix-tinted
#       cursor shapes at 24, 32, 48 px hotspot variants.
#   Backlog issue filed per T10 instructions.
#   Upstream cursor fallback: Adwaita (GNOME project, LGPL-2.1+).
#   This index.theme file: original Orion-X project work.

[Icon Theme]
Name=Orion-X-Cursor
Comment=Orion-X cyberdeck cursor theme (Adwaita inheritance placeholder; polish deferred)
Inherits=Adwaita
